## Appendix B: Sandbox and lifecycle chaos suite (exit gate for phase 1)

| Test | Expected result |
|---|---|
| `process.exit(1)` during `query` | Call → `2005`; one retry on a new instance succeeds; no effect on the host |
| `while(true){}` in `load` | Load timeout → FAILED → backoff; the 5th failure → QUARANTINED + alert |
| Allocate 4 GB | OOM kill contained by the cgroup; other instances unaffected |
| Fork bomb | `pids.max` stops it; instance recycled |
| `fetch("http://169.254.169.254")` / an RFC1918 address / a host not on the allowlist | Connection refused by the proxy; audit event |
| DNS rebinding of an allowlisted name to 10.0.0.5 | Blocked when the proxy re-resolves |
| `host/data.query` from a `setTimeout` after the call returns | `2008 InvalidCallToken` |
| Reading `/proc/1/environ` or the host filesystem, writing outside `/tmp` | Nothing sensitive present / EROFS |
| Output doesn't match `describe` | `2009 SchemaMismatch` |
| Reload to a version whose `load` throws | Old version keeps serving; `reloadFailed`; zero dropped requests |
| Reload under 200 rps of load | Zero failed requests; in-flight streams finish on the old instance; each `runId` stays on one version |
| Visualization runs `parent.document`, `fetch()` or `document.cookie` | Blocked by the opaque origin and CSP |
| Revoke while 50 instances are running | All killed within 60 s; installations fall back or go to REVOKED |

---

**Before phase 0 starts, settle two things:**
- **D1 (deployment target):** it decides how the Supervisor starts sandboxes.
- **D2 (instance density):** one instance per workspace could get expensive.

