## 1. Architecture overview

```
┌──────────────────────────────── Host process ─────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                               │
│  Report Engine ──► Extension Router ──► Plugin Registry (runtime)             │
│                         │                   ▲    │                            │
│                         │                   │    └─ Contribution Index        │
│                         ▼                   │                                 │
│                   Lifecycle Manager ────────┘                                 │
│                         │                                                     │
│                         ▼                                                     │
│                  Sandbox Supervisor ──── Capability Broker ──► Secrets, KV,   │
│                         │                    ▲                 Egress Proxy,  │
│                         │                    │                 Data Service,  │
└─────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────── Telemetry ─────┘
          framed RPC (fd3)│                    │ capability calls
┌─────────────────────────▼────────────────────┴───┐   ┌──────────────────────┐
│ Sandbox process: plugin runtime + plugin bundle  │   │ Package Registry svc │
│   (one per plugin version; optionally per tenant)│   │ (publish/sign/store) │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────┘
```

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **Package Registry service** | Stores signed plugin packages and version history. Handles publish, promotion (channels), and yank. |
| **Plugin Registry (runtime)** | Tracks what is installed and running in this host: records, states, per-tenant enablement, contribution index. |
| **Lifecycle Manager** | Runs load/unload/reload. Owns the state machine, dependency order, drain, and version pinning. |
| **Sandbox Supervisor** | Spawns and kills sandbox processes, applies resource limits, restarts with backoff, quarantines. |
| **Capability Broker** | The only path from plugin code to side effects. Authorizes each call as manifest grants ∩ invoking user's permissions. |
| **Extension Router** | Turns engine requests ("run data source X") into RPC invocations. Handles deadlines, cancellation, streaming. |
| **Plugin SDK** | Library the teams use: typed contract, `definePlugin`, test harness, CLI. |

