## 2. Package format and manifest

### 2.1 Package layout (`.rplug` = gzip'd tar)

```
plugin.json          # manifest (required)
dist/index.mjs       # single bundled ESM entry; no runtime npm install
dist/**              # other bundled assets referenced by entry
assets/icon.svg      # optional
sbom.spdx.json       # required for publish (generated by `rplug pack`)
CHANGELOG.md         # required for publish
```

The registry, not the package, stores the package digest (sha256) and signature (§3.4). Both are checked at install time and again at load time.

### 2.2 Manifest rules
- **Strict validation.** Unknown top-level keys are rejected unless they start with `x-`. The manifest controls security, so an old host must refuse a new permission field it doesn't understand instead of silently ignoring it. (Runtime payloads work the other way and are tolerant, see §6.2.)
- `manifestVersion` is an integer and changes only when the manifest format itself breaks. It is separate from `apiVersion`.
- IDs are reverse-DNS and globally unique: `com.<company>.<team>.<name>`. Contribution IDs are unique within their plugin. They are referenced as `<pluginId>/<contributionId>`.

