## 2. Package and manifest

### 2.1 Package (`.rplug`, a tar.gz)
```
plugin.json        manifest (required)
dist/index.mjs     single bundled ESM entry; no runtime npm install
assets/            optional
sbom.spdx.json     required to publish
CHANGELOG.md       required to publish
```
The digest (sha256) and signature are stored in the registry. The host checks them at install and again at every load.

### 2.2 Rules
- **Validation is strict.** Unknown top-level keys are rejected unless they start with `x-`. The manifest controls security, so an old host must refuse a permission field it doesn't understand rather than silently ignore it. Runtime payloads are the opposite: they tolerate unknown fields (§6.2).
- `manifestVersion` is an integer and only changes when the manifest format itself breaks. It is separate from `apiVersion`.
- Plugin IDs are reverse-DNS and each team owns a prefix: `com.<company>.<team>.<name>`. A contribution is referenced as `<pluginId>/<contributionId>`.

### 2.3 JSON Schema (manifestVersion 1)

```json
