### 6.5 SDK error classes

`ConfigError(issues)`, `AuthError`, `RetryableError(retryAfterMs?)`, `NotSupportedError`, `PermissionDeniedError`. Any other thrown error becomes `PLUGIN_ERROR`. Its message is kept, and its stack trace is logged but never shown to users.

### 6.6 Error codes (wire)

| Code | Name | Set by | Retry? |
|------|------|--------|--------|
| -32001 | `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` | host | caller decides |
| -32002 | `CANCELLED` | host | no |
| -32003 | `PERMISSION_DENIED` | host | no |
| -32004 | `CONFIG_INVALID` | plugin/host | no |
| -32005 | `NOT_SUPPORTED` | plugin/host | no |
| -32006 | `RETRYABLE` | plugin | yes, honor `retryAfterMs` |
| -32007 | `AUTH_FAILED` (upstream credentials) | plugin | after reauth |
| -32008 | `PLUGIN_ERROR` | plugin | no |
| -32009 | `PLUGIN_CRASHED` | host | yes, once |
| -32010 | `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` | host | yes, with backoff |
| -32011 | `CONTRACT_VIOLATION` (invalid plugin output) | host | no |
| -32012 | `UNAVAILABLE` (disabled/quarantined/failed) | host | no |

