```

### 6.5 Errors

**SDK classes:** `ConfigError(issues)`, `AuthError`, `RetryableError(retryAfterMs?)`, `NotSupportedError`, `PermissionDeniedError`. Anything else thrown becomes `PLUGIN_ERROR`. Its stack trace is logged but never shown to users.

**Wire error codes**

| Code | Name | Set by | Retry |
|---|---|---|---|
| -32001 | `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` | host | caller decides |
| -32002 | `CANCELLED` | host | no |
| -32003 | `PERMISSION_DENIED` | host | no |
| -32004 | `CONFIG_INVALID` | plugin/host | no |
| -32005 | `NOT_SUPPORTED` | plugin/host | no |
| -32006 | `RETRYABLE` | plugin | yes, honor `retryAfterMs` |
| -32007 | `AUTH_FAILED` (upstream) | plugin | after reauth |
| -32008 | `PLUGIN_ERROR` | plugin | no |
| -32009 | `PLUGIN_CRASHED` | host | once |
| -32010 | `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` | host | with backoff |
| -32011 | `CONTRACT_VIOLATION` | host | no |
| -32012 | `UNAVAILABLE` (disabled/quarantined/failed) | host | no |

