### 4.3 Validation rules beyond JSON Schema

The CLI and registry run these checks. Each failure has a stable error code so teams can fix things in CI.

| Code | Rule |
|---|---|
| `M001` | Contribution IDs and aliases are unique within the plugin. |
| `M002` | Every `eventHandlers[].event` is listed in `permissions.events.subscribe`. |
| `M003` | Every config field with `x-secret: true` is listed in `permissions.secrets`, and vice versa. |
| `M004` | `engines.api` resolves to at least one API version the target host supports. |
| `M005` | `runtime.entry` exists in the package, and every referenced path stays inside the package (no `..`). |
| `M006` | `network[].host` is not `*`, not an IP literal, and not in the platform deny list (metadata endpoints, host control plane). |
| `M007` | `paramsVersion` did not decrease compared with the previously published version of this plugin. |
| `M008` | No contribution ID from the previous published version disappeared unless the major version increased or it moved into `aliases`. |
| `M009` | `id` publisher prefix equals `publisher`, and the package signature belongs to that publisher. |
| `M010` | `limits` are within platform maximums. Values above them are warnings at pack time and errors at publish time. |

### 4.4 Manifest evolution

`manifestVersion` is independent of the API version. New optional fields can be added to manifest v1 without a new version. Removing or re-meaning a field requires `manifestVersion: 2`. The host reads every manifest version it has ever accepted, and the CLI can migrate manifests with `rpt-plugin manifest migrate`.

