## 12. Delivery plan for next quarter

The contract has to stabilize before the platform is finished, so teams can build against the SDK and harness while the sandbox and registry harden.

| Week | Platform milestone | Plugin teams can |
|------|--------------------|------------------|
| 0–1 | Resolve §0 assumptions and §13 decisions with all five teams. Review the contribution interfaces against each team's first plugin. | Bring concrete use cases; confirm contribution types |
| 2–3 | **API 1.0.0-rc.1**: TypeSpec contract, generated types, manifest schema v1, SDK and `rplug init/validate/dev` on the local harness (no OS sandbox) | Start building against the harness |
| 4–6 | Registry, catalog, and signing. Supervisor with full lifecycle (§5). Broker with network, secrets, storage, and data enforcement. Conformance kit. | Run the conformance kit in CI; file contract issues |
| 7 | **API 1.0.0 freeze.** Breaking changes after this need an explicit exception. | Target `^1.0.0` |
| 7–9 | Production sandbox (gVisor, cgroups, egress), iframe UI sandbox, host compatibility CI, observability and status pages | Deploy to staging with real isolation |
| 10–11 | Security review, load and chaos tests (crash loops, reload under load, OOM), runbooks | Fix sandbox-only issues; beta with pilot tenants |
| 12–13 | GA: publishing to production, admin approval UI | Production launch |

Top risks: (1) contribution interfaces don't fit a team's use case, which is mitigated by the week 0–1 review against real plugins; (2) gVisor adds too much overhead for streaming Arrow data, which should be benchmarked in week 4 with nsjail as the fallback; (3) cold start latency under lazy activation, mitigated by pre-warming `onStartup` or high-traffic plugins per tenant.

