## 1. Architecture overview

```
                           ┌──────────────────────── Host ────────────────────────┐
  CI / rplug publish ────▶ │  Catalog ──▶ Registry (per-tenant installs, grants)  │
  Report engine / UI ────▶ │  Contribution Router ──▶ Supervisor ──▶ Instance Pool│
                           │                 Capability Broker                    │
                           │        (http, secrets, storage, data, log, metrics)  │
                           └───────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                                           │ framed RPC over UDS, one OS sandbox per instance
                           ┌───────────────┴─────────────────────┐
                           │ Plugin Instance: plugin-runtime ◀─▶ plugin code │ x N
                           └─────────────────────────────────────┘
  Browser report page ──postMessage──▶ sandboxed iframe (visualization UI bundle)
```

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **Catalog** | Stores immutable artifacts, keyed by sha256. Checks manifests, signatures, and API compatibility when a plugin is published. |
| **Registry** | Tracks installs per tenant: pinned version, permissions an admin granted, config, and enabled state. It is the single source of truth for what should run. |
| **Contribution Router** | Maps an ID like `com.acme.sf/salesforce` to a running instance, and starts the instance on first use. |
| **Supervisor** | Runs the lifecycle state machine: spawning, health checks, draining, blue/green reload, crash backoff, quarantine. |
| **Capability Broker** | The host side of every host API call. Enforces grants, quotas, rate limits, and the calling user's identity. It is the plugin's only way to reach the outside world. |
| **plugin-runtime** | Host-owned code inside the sandbox. It runs the handshake and protocol, then loads the plugin. Plugin authors never write it. |
| **SDK** | `@reporting/plugin-sdk`, which re-exports the types in `@reporting/plugin-api`. |

---

## 2. Extension points

| Type | Purpose | Runs in | Idempotent |
|---|---|---|---|
| `dataSource` | Connect, discover schema, stream query results as record batches | server sandbox | yes |
| `transform` | Turn record batches into new record batches | server sandbox | yes |
| `visualization` | Optional server `prepare` step plus a client render bundle | server + browser iframe | yes |
| `exporter` | Turn a report snapshot into a file stream (PDF, XLSX, ...) | server sandbox | yes |
| `delivery` | Send an exported file to email, Slack, SFTP, ... | server sandbox | **no** (host supplies an idempotency key) |

A contribution's full ID is `<pluginId>/<contributionId>`. Saved reports store that ID, the plugin's major version, and the contribution's `configVersion`.

