## 10. Delivery plan (to have teams productive next quarter)

Plugin teams must build against a **frozen API 1.0-rc** from week 1. Platform work that stays invisible to them (OS sandbox, multi-node registry) can ship behind the contract.

| Phase | Weeks | Platform deliverables | Plugin teams can |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 — Contract freeze | 1–3 | Manifest v1 schema, API 1.0-rc schemas + generated TS types, SDK, `rpt-plugin init/validate/dev/test`, TCK v1.0-rc, 1 reference plugin per kind | Scaffold, build, test locally against mock host |
| 1 — Runtime | 3–7 | Lifecycle manager (load/unload, crash handling), process sandbox + broker + invocation binding, JSON-RPC + Arrow transport, catalog + installation registry, staging deploy | Deploy to staging tenants, run end-to-end |
| 2 — Hardening | 6–10 | gVisor/nsjail confinement, cgroups, egress proxy with IP checks, signed publishing, permission approval, UI iframe sandbox + headless print, dashboards/alerts | Pass `--sandbox` TCK in CI, request approvals |
| 3 — GA | 10–12 | Blue/green reload with state transfer, config migration, kill switch, runbooks, **API 1.0 GA** (breaking changes from rc allowed only with all 5 teams' sign-off) | Ship to production tenants |

API governance from week 1:
- Changes go through a lightweight RFC in `plugin-api/rfcs`.
- Every API change is reviewed by one platform engineer and at least one plugin team.
- Weekly office hours.
- Each of the five teams names an API liaison.

