## 0. Assumptions and open decisions

No existing codebase was available when this was written, so the design rests on the assumptions below. Settle each one before the contract freezes (§11).

| # | Assumption | If it's wrong |
|---|------------|---------------|
| A1 | The host backend is TypeScript on Node.js (≥ 22 LTS) and the frontend is a web app. | The wire protocol (§8.4) and manifest don't depend on the language. Only the SDK and the in-process runtime shim change. |
| A2 | The tool is multi-tenant SaaS. | On-prem single-tenant makes things simpler: tenancy scoping (§7.6) turns into a no-op. |
| A3 | Plugins come from internal teams now, but third-party plugins are possible later. | The sandbox is built for code that is buggy or compromised, not for determined attackers (§7.1). Hostile third-party code needs the `container`/microVM driver. |
| A4 | Data volumes are large enough that row-by-row JSON is too slow. | Arrow IPC (§8.5) can be swapped for JSON batches. |
