## 4. Manifest schema

### 4.1 Packaging

A plugin ships as a `.rptplugin` file, which is a gzip tarball:

```
manifest.json          # required, validated against the schema below
dist/backend/index.js  # backend entry (bundled, ESM, no node_modules resolution at runtime)
dist/ui/index.html     # optional, visualization UI entry
assets/                # icons, localization bundles
CHECKSUMS.sha256       # sha256 of every file
SIGNATURE              # detached signature over CHECKSUMS.sha256 (§5.6)
```

Backend code must be one self-contained bundle. The runtime doesn't resolve dependencies and doesn't run `npm install`, which removes install-time supply-chain execution.

### 4.2 Example manifest

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.rpt.internal/plugin-manifest/1.json",
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "acme.warehouse",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "displayName": "Acme Warehouse Connector",
  "description": "Query the Acme Postgres warehouse.",
  "publisher": { "team": "data-platform", "contact": "data-platform@acme.internal" },
  "license": "Proprietary",

  "engines": { "hostApi": "^2.1.0" },

  "runtime": {
    "backend": { "entry": "dist/backend/index.js", "kind": "node" },
    "ui": { "entry": "dist/ui/index.html" }
  },

  "activation": ["onDataSource:postgres", "onCommand:refresh-catalog"],

  "contributes": {
    "dataSources": [
      {
        "id": "postgres",
        "displayName": "Acme Postgres",
        "configSchema": { "$ref": "#/definitions/pgConfig" },
        "supportsPushdown": ["filter", "projection", "limit"]
      }
    ],
    "commands": [
      { "id": "refresh-catalog", "title": "Refresh catalog", "context": ["dataSource"] }
    ]
  },

  "capabilities": [
    { "name": "net:fetch", "hosts": ["warehouse.acme.internal:5432"] },
