## 13. Assumptions to confirm (each changes part of the design)

1. **Host stack is TypeScript/Node, server-side.** If the host is JVM or .NET, the process boundary, manifest and wire protocol stay the same. Only the host implementation changes, and the Node plugin SDK stays.
2. **Deployment is Linux containers or Kubernetes.** On-prem Windows or desktop deployment would change sandbox layers 2–3 (Job Objects and Windows Firewall rules instead).
