## 4. Registry

The registry has two layers: the **Package Catalog** (what exists) and the **Runtime Registry** (what is installed and running where).

### 4.1 Data model

```
plugin_publisher(id PK, display_name, owners[], created_at)

plugin_package(
  plugin_id, version,                      -- PK (plugin_id, version)
  publisher_id FK, manifest JSONB, manifest_version INT,
  api_range, host_range, runtime,
  artifact_uri, sha256, size_bytes,
  signature, signing_key_id, sbom_uri,
  review_status ENUM(pending, approved, rejected),
  status ENUM(published, deprecated, yanked, revoked),
  status_reason, published_at, published_by)

plugin_installation(
  id PK, workspace_id, plugin_id, version,  -- exact pin
  enabled BOOL,
  granted_permissions JSONB,               -- snapshot at approval time
  pending_permissions JSONB NULL,          -- awaiting admin approval on upgrade
  update_policy ENUM(none, patch, minor),
  config_ref, service_identity_id,
  previous_version NULL,                   -- rollback target
  storage_snapshot_ref NULL,               -- pre-migration snapshot
  installed_by, updated_at,
  UNIQUE(workspace_id, plugin_id))

contribution_index(
  fqid, workspace_id, kind, plugin_id, version,
  display_name, options_schema_version, metadata JSONB,   -- from manifest
  available BOOL,                                         -- false if disabled/quarantined
  PK (workspace_id, fqid))

plugin_instance(                           -- live state; in-memory + replicated (e.g. Redis)
  instance_id PK, installation_id, generation INT,
  state, node_id, pid, started_at,
  crash_count_window, last_error, last_health)

plugin_audit_log(ts, workspace_id, plugin_id, actor, action, details JSONB)
```

The editor and report engine read `contribution_index` to list and validate contributions **without activating plugins**.

### 4.2 Publish pipeline (Catalog)
```
upload ─► unpack (size cap, no symlinks, path traversal check)
       ─► manifest JSON Schema + semantic validation (§3.3)
       ─► verify signature (publisher key, KMS-backed) + sha256
       ─► publisher ownership check; version must not already exist (immutable)
       ─► static checks: bundle size, no native addons (unless runtime allows),
          dependency vuln scan, SBOM generation
       ─► TCK smoke run in a real sandbox against every supported API minor in range
       ─► permission diff vs previous version → flags "needs review" if broadened
       ─► review_status = pending|approved (auto-approve if no permission broadening
          and publisher is internal-trusted)
       ─► status = published
```
- **Yank:** new installs are blocked. Existing installs keep running and show a warning.
- **Revoke** (security issue): the host disables all installations within one reconcile cycle and records the reason.

### 4.3 Install and upgrade resolution
```
resolve(workspace, pluginId, requested):
  candidates = catalog versions matching requested, status=published, review=approved
  for v in candidates (highest first):
    require host.version ∈ v.host_range
    require host.supportedApi ∩ v.api_range ≠ ∅
    require v.runtime ∈ host.runtimes
    for each required service: some installed (or co-installed) provider satisfies range
    require dependency graph acyclic
    require limits within workspace policy
    → pick v
  permissionsDelta = v.permissions − installation.granted_permissions
  if permissionsDelta ≠ ∅: set pending_permissions; stop until admin approves
  else: commit installation(version=v, previous_version=old) → Lifecycle.upgrade()
```
- **Auto-update** (`update_policy`) runs this resolution on a schedule. It never auto-approves broader permissions.
- **Rollback** swaps `version` and `previous_version`. If a storage migration ran, it also restores `storage_snapshot_ref` (§5.5).
- **Uninstall** is blocked while saved reports reference the plugin's contributions, unless `force=true`. With force, those blocks show a "plugin unavailable" placeholder. Storage is kept for 30 days unless `purge=true`.

### 4.4 Admin API
```
POST   /api/plugins/packages                                  publish (multipart)
GET    /api/plugins/packages/{id}/versions
POST   /api/plugins/packages/{id}/versions/{v}:yank|:revoke|:approve
POST   /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins                           install {id, version|range, updatePolicy}
GET    /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins[/{id}]                    includes instance health
PATCH  /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}                      {enabled, config, version}
POST   /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}:approve-permissions
POST   /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}:reload
POST   /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}:rollback
POST   /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}:unquarantine
DELETE /api/workspaces/{ws}/plugins/{id}?force=&purge=
GET    /api/workspaces/{ws}/contributions?kind=
```
Every change writes to `plugin_audit_log`.

