## 3. Manifest (`plugin.json`)

The host must be able to list, validate, permission-check and place a plugin in the editor **without running its code**.

### 3.1 Example
```json
{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "sales-eng.salesforce",
  "version": "1.4.2",
  "displayName": "Salesforce",
  "publisher": { "id": "sales-eng", "team": "Sales Engineering", "contact": "sales-eng@corp.example" },
  "apiVersion": "^1.2.0",
  "engines": { "host": ">=4.8.0 <6", "runtime": "node22" },
  "main": "dist/server.js",
