## 13. Delivery plan (13 weeks)

| Weeks | Platform | Plugin teams |
|---|---|---|
| 0–2 | Manifest v1 and **API 1.0-rc** IDL; generated types; mock-host testkit; `init`/`validate` | Review the RFC; scaffold against the mock host |
| 2–5 | Registry, lifecycle (load/unload/crash), `linux-process` and `dev-local` drivers, broker (http, storage, secret injection, data), protocol, `rpt-plugin dev` | Build core logic on the mock host |
| 5–7 | **Pilot:** one datasource team end to end in staging; publish pipeline with signing; TCK v1. **API 1.0 GA freeze at the end of week 7** | Pilot team ships to staging; the others give rc feedback |
| 7–10 | Overlap and drain-first reload with migrations; iframe runtime and static export; exporter, action and events; services broker; approval UI; dashboards | All teams integrate on the real host |
| 10–13 | Chaos tests (kill -9, OOM, hang, malformed frames, slow egress), upgrade and rollback drills, quarantine flows, docs, runbooks | TCK green; staged production rollout behind a flag |

**Exit criteria**
- All five plugins pass the TCK.
- Killing any plugin mid-run still leaves the other report blocks rendered.
- Upgrade and rollback of every plugin cause no failed report runs with overlap, and ≤30s of queueing with drain-first.

**Main risks and mitigations**

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| API churn after the freeze | Two-week rc review and a pilot team first |
| Arrow is new to the teams | SDK helpers |
| Static export throughput | Render pool plus a cache keyed by (fqid, options hash, data hash) |

