## 2. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Plugin** | A versioned unit of functionality with one manifest, owned by one team. |
| **Package** | A signed `.rpx` archive containing the manifest, the bundled code and metadata. |
| **Contribution point** | A host-defined extension slot, e.g. `dataSources` or `exporters`. |
| **Contribution** | One concrete entry a plugin adds to a point, e.g. a Snowflake data source. It is fully qualified as `<pluginId>/<contributionId>`. |
| **Capability** | A permission to use a brokered resource: secrets, storage, data, network destinations or services. |
| **Grant** | The capabilities an admin approved for one plugin version. |
| **Generation** | One running instance set of one plugin version. It increments on every (re)load. |
| **Isolation unit** | The scope that shares a sandbox process: `per-tenant` by default, or `shared`. |
| **Host API version** | The semver of the contract surface (protocol methods, handler interfaces, data types). |
| **Invocation** | One host→plugin call to a contribution handler. It carries an invocation context. |

