## 13. Decisions and rejected alternatives
| Decision | Chosen | Rejected, and why |
|---|---|---|
| Execution boundary | OS process plus OS-level confinement | **In-process `vm` or worker threads:** not a security boundary, and one crash affects everything. **A container per plugin:** seconds of cold start and more to operate; kept as the path for third-party plugins. **WASM:** the JS DB-driver and PDF ecosystems don't work there yet; worth revisiting for `functions`. |
| Network control | Network namespace, egress proxy, policy DNS | **Host-provided `fetch` only:** doesn't cover database protocols, and plugins could bypass it with raw sockets. |
| Wire format | JSON-RPC for control, Arrow for bulk data | **gRPC:** a heavier toolchain and harder to debug, and bulk data would still need Arrow. |
| Dependencies | Service interfaces | **Plugin-ID dependencies:** tie teams' release cycles together and prevent swapping providers. |
| Reload | Side-by-side generations with run pinning | **Stop then start:** users see failures, and a single report can mix plugin versions. |
| Declaring contributions | Manifest plus a handler check | **Registration at runtime only:** the host couldn't list or approve plugins without running their code. |

