## 6. Configuration and secrets

| Kind | Set by | Schema | Stored | Delivered |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Plugin config | Admin | `configSchema` | `plugin_record.admin_config_json` | `ctx.config`, plus `onConfigChange` |
| Contribution config (connection, params, options, target) | Report author | The contribution's schema | `saved_contrib_cfg` | Passed as the argument of each call |
| Plugin secrets | Admin, in the vault | Names listed in `capabilities.secrets` | Host vault | `ctx.secrets.get(name)` at call time |
| Secret fields in contribution config (`x-secret: true`) | Report author | The contribution's schema | Host vault; the config row stores only a vault reference | Resolved into the call argument, and never returned by any read API |

The host validates all config before delivering it. Plugins may assume the config they receive
conforms to their schema.

