    "storage": { "kv": { "quotaMb": 20 } }
  },
  "resources": { "memoryMb": 512, "cpuMillicores": 1000, "maxConcurrency": 16, "maxInstances": 2,
                 "timeouts": { "invocationMs": 300000, "drainMs": 120000 } },
  "lifecycle": { "hotReload": "stateful", "stateSchemaVersion": 2 }
}
```

### 3.4 Semantic validation rules

`rpt validate`, the registry at publish, and the host at install all enforce these.

| # | Rule |
|---|---|
| V1 | Contribution IDs are unique across all kinds within a plugin. |
| V2 | Every referenced path exists inside the artifact. No symlinks. |
| V3 | Embedded schemas are valid JSON Schema 2020-12 using the allowed keyword subset, with no remote `$ref`, and are no larger than 64 KiB. |
| V4 | `engines.pluginApi` overlaps the API versions the host supports, checked at publish and again at install. |
| V5 | The declared SDK version implements an API version that satisfies `engines.pluginApi`. |
| V6 | Egress rules use no IP literals. A wildcard covers one label only, and never an apex such as `*.com`. `fromConfig` must point at a string property with `format: hostname`. |
| V7 | `tenancy: shared` needs a platform security approval flag on the release. |
| V8 | The dependency graph has no cycles, and every dependency exists in the registry. |
| V9 | A new version must be higher than every published version. Versions are never overwritten; use yank instead. |
| V10 | `hotReload: stateful` requires `stateSchemaVersion` (also enforced in the schema). |
| V11 | The ID namespace `com.acme.<team>.` must match `publisher.team` and the identity that signed the release. |
| V12 | The registry computes a permission diff against the previous release and attaches it; the diff drives re-approval (§4.6). |
| V13 | Resource requests stay within platform maximums. |
| V14 | A field annotated `x-rpt-since: 1.N` requires `engines.pluginApi` ≥ 1.N. |
| V15 | `configSchemaVersion` never goes down. If it goes up, `MigrateConfig` must handle every earlier version, which the conformance kit checks with fixtures from previous releases. |

**Secrets never go in config.** Plugins declare secret names; tenant admins bind values from the vault. The host builds config forms from `configSchema` and uses the `x-rpt-*` hints.

**`manifestVersion` evolution.** It only increments for breaking manifest changes, and additive fields use `x-rpt-since`. The registry upconverts older manifests to the internal model and never downconverts.

