### 5.3 Schema

This is the readable form. The JSON Schema I drafted matches it field for field, including conditional rules such as "`runtime` is required if there are server-side contributions".

```ts
interface PluginManifest {
  $schema?: string;
  manifestVersion: 1;
  id: string;                 // "<publisher>.<name>"  /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,31}\.[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$/
  version: string;            // semver
  displayName: string;        // ≤ 80
  description?: string;       // ≤ 500
  icon?: PackagePath;
  repository?: string;
  license?: string;
  publisher: { id: string; name: string; contact: string /* email */; oncall?: string };
  engines: { reportingApi: string };                       // semver range, e.g. "^1.2.0"

  runtime?: { type: "node"; version: "22" | "24"; entry: PackagePath };  // required if any server contribution or provided service
  ui?: { entry: PackagePath; styles?: PackagePath };                       // required if visualizations

  activation?: { mode?: "lazy" | "eager"; idleShutdownSeconds?: number };  // lazy; 600 (60–86400)
  tenancy?: "isolated" | "shared";                                         // isolated; shared needs review
  config?: ConfigDeclaration;                                              // installation-level, set by tenant admin
  storage?: { schemaVersion: number; kv?: { quotaMB?: number } };          // quota 10 (1–1024)
  permissions?: {
    network?: {
      egress?: { host: string; ports: number[]; purpose: string }[];       // "api.x.com" | "*.x.com" | "${config.host}"
      privateNetwork?: boolean;                                            // needs an admin grant plus admin-supplied CIDRs
    };
    data?: { query?: boolean };                                            // query host datasets as the invoker
    notifications?: { send?: boolean };
  };
  limits?: {                                                               // requested; capped by trust tier
    memoryMB?: number; cpu?: number; tmpMB?: number;                       // 256, 0.5, 64
    maxConcurrentInvocations?: number;                                     // 4
    invocationTimeoutSeconds?: number; activationTimeoutSeconds?: number;  // 60, 15
  };
  upgrade?: { strategy?: "rolling" | "drain-first"; drainTimeoutSeconds?: number };  // rolling, 30
  services?: {
    provides?: { id: string; version: string; description?: string }[];   // id "<publisher>.<name>"
    requires?: { id: string; range: string; optional?: boolean }[];
  };
  contributes: {                                                           // at least one entry
    dataSources?: DataSourceDecl[];  transforms?: TransformDecl[];
    visualizations?: VisualizationDecl[];  exporters?: ExporterDecl[];
    deliveryChannels?: DeliveryChannelDecl[];  jobs?: JobDecl[];
  };
}

type PackagePath = string;    // relative POSIX path; no "..", no leading "/", no backslashes
interface ConfigDeclaration {
  version: number;            // integer ≥ 1; bump on incompatible change, supply migrateConfig
  schema: object;             // JSON Schema 2020-12, type "object"; "x-secret": true; "x-ui" hints
}
interface ContributionDecl {
  id: string;                 // /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$/, unique across all types in the plugin
  displayName: string; description?: string; icon?: PackagePath;
  config?: ConfigDeclaration; // per-use config saved inside reports; secrets not allowed
  deprecated?: { message: string; replacement?: string };
}
interface DataSourceDecl extends ContributionDecl {
  capabilities?: {
    schemaDiscovery?: boolean; incremental?: boolean;
    pushdown?: ("project" | "filter" | "sort" | "limit" | "aggregate")[];
    filterOperators?: ("eq"|"neq"|"lt"|"lte"|"gt"|"gte"|"in"|"notIn"|"isNull"|"isNotNull"|"contains"|"startsWith"|"between")[];
    aggregateFunctions?: ("count"|"countDistinct"|"sum"|"avg"|"min"|"max")[];
  };
}
interface TransformDecl extends ContributionDecl { inputs?: { min?: number; max?: number }; deterministic?: boolean }
interface VisualizationDecl extends ContributionDecl {
  dataRoles: { id: string; displayName: string; kind: "dimension" | "measure" | "any"; types?: DataType[]; min?: number; max?: number }[];
  imageExport?: ("png" | "svg")[]; interactions?: ("select" | "drilldown" | "tooltip")[]; maxRows?: number;  // 50,000
}
interface ExporterDecl extends ContributionDecl { formats: { id: string; mimeType: string; extension: string; displayName: string }[] }
interface DeliveryChannelDecl extends ContributionDecl {
  attachments?: { supported?: boolean; maxTotalMB?: number };
  recipientKinds?: ("user" | "group" | "address" | "channel")[];
}
interface JobDecl extends ContributionDecl {
  triggers: ({ type: "schedule"; defaultCron: string; adminConfigurable?: boolean; minIntervalSeconds?: number }
           | { type: "event"; event: "report.published" | "report.deleted" | "dataset.refreshed" | "delivery.failed" })[];
}
type DataType = "string"|"integer"|"number"|"decimal"|"boolean"|"date"|"timestamp"|"duration"|"json"|"binary";
```

**There are two levels of config.**
- **Installation config** is set once per tenant by an admin: credentials, account IDs. It is the only place secrets are allowed.
- **Contribution config** is set per use by report authors and saved inside reports. If a plugin needs several connections, list them as named entries in the installation config, and have contribution config refer to them by name. Report authors never handle secrets.

### 5.4 Semantic validation

`rpt-plugin validate` and the registry both check these rules, which JSON Schema can't express:
1. The prefix of `id` equals `publisher.id`, and the uploading team owns that publisher namespace.
2. `version` is higher than every version already published, and is never reused, even after a yank.
3. `engines.reportingApi` is a valid range that includes an API version the host supports. It must also accept the API version of the bundled SDK.
4. Contribution IDs are unique within the plugin. Entry and icon files exist.
5. The entry file is loaded inside a validation sandbox. It must export exactly the contributions and services the manifest declares, no more and no fewer.
6. Every config schema is valid 2020-12 with `type: "object"`. `x-secret` appears only on string fields, and only in installation config.
7. `config.version` and `storage.schemaVersion` never decrease. If a config schema changed incompatibly, the version must be bumped. `migrateConfig` must cover every older config version that saved reports in any tenant still use (the registry checks the reference table, §7.6).
8. A `${config.x}` in an egress rule must point to an existing non-secret string field.
9. Limits must stay within the trust tier's maximums. `tenancy: "shared"`, `activation.mode: "eager"` and `privateNetwork` all trigger a review.
10. `services.provides` IDs use the plugin's own publisher prefix, and the graph of required services has no cycles.
11. Removing a contribution that the previous version had requires a major plugin version bump. Before install, admins see which saved reports would be affected.
12. Cron expressions parse, and schedules respect `minIntervalSeconds`.

### 5.5 Permissions and grants

| Permission | How it's granted | Enforced by |
|---|---|---|
| `network.egress` (public hosts) | Shown at install; granted automatically for the internal tier | Per-instance network namespace firewall with DNS pinning |
| `network.privateNetwork` | Explicit admin grant per installation, with CIDRs chosen by the admin | Firewall |
| `data.query` | Admin grant | Broker, which acts as the invoker |
| `notifications.send` | Admin grant | Broker, rate-limited |
| `storage.kv` | Automatic, within quota | Broker quota |
| `services.requires` | Automatic if the provider is installed for the tenant | Broker |

**Permission expansion never happens silently.** If a new version asks for more than the installation has granted, the installation stays on the old version with status `awaiting-grant` until an admin approves.

