# Reporting Tool Plugin Architecture (v1)

## 1. Overview

```
 ┌──────────────────────────── Control plane ────────────────────────────┐
 │  Catalog (published packages)   Installations (per env/tenant)        │
 │  Permission grants   Config & secret refs   Audit log   Kill switch   │
 └───────────────▲──────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┘
      publish    │                                  │ desired state (watch)
 ┌───────────────┴──┐              ┌────────────────▼──── Host node ───────────────────┐
 │ rpt-plugin CLI   │              │ Reconciler → Resolver → Supervisor                 │
 │ (validate/sign)  │              │                           │ spawn/kill/route        │
 └──────────────────┘              │ Report engine ─► Contribution Index ─► Router      │
                                   │                              │  RPC (inherited fd) │
                                   │  Capability Broker ◄─────────┤                     │
                                   │  (http, secrets, data, kv)   ▼                     │
                                   │              ┌─ sandbox proc: plugin A v1.4 ─┐    │
                                   │              ├─ sandbox proc: plugin B v2.0 ─┤    │
                                   └──────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴────┘
 Browser: report UI ─► <iframe sandbox> custom visualizations (separate origin, postMessage RPC)
```

**Core rules:**
1. **Plugins have no ambient authority.** Every network call, secret read, data query and storage access goes through a host broker that checks the grant and the calling user (principal).
2. **Plugins run outside the host process by default.** A crash, memory leak or infinite loop in one team's plugin can never take down report rendering.
3. **The manifest is the whole promise.** Anything a plugin does must be declared, and anything declared must actually be registered at activation.
4. **The API is batched.** No per-row callbacks cross the process boundary; data moves as Apache Arrow record batches.
5. **The host validates everything a plugin returns** against the contract schema. Plugin output is untrusted input.

## 2. Extension points (contribution types)

| Type | Runs | What it does | Invoked by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `dataSources` | server sandbox | Connects to external data; `describe`, `plan` (optional pushdown), `query` → Arrow stream | Report data layer |
| `transforms` | server sandbox | 1..8 input datasets → 1 output dataset | Report pipeline |
| `visualizations` (`spec`) | server sandbox | Data + field bindings → Vega-Lite spec | Renderer |
| `visualizations` (`custom`) | browser iframe | Draws into a sandboxed iframe | Report UI |
| `exporters` | server sandbox | Resolved report → byte stream (PDF, XLSX…) | Export/delivery |
| `commands` | server sandbox | User-triggered actions on toolbar, context menu, admin console or API | UI / API |
| `scheduledJobs` | server sandbox | Cron-driven background work, global or per tenant | Scheduler |
| `services` | server sandbox | Typed RPC interface other plugins can call | Other plugins (via host) |

**Out of scope for v1:** auth providers, plugins that change other plugins or core report behavior (events are observe-only), native addons, in-process execution for anything other than host-bundled code.

## 3. Manifest schema (`plugin.json`, `manifestVersion: 1`)

The source of truth is a TypeBox definition in `@reporting/plugin-api`. The JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) is generated from it and published at a stable URL, so editors autocomplete. All objects are closed (`additionalProperties: false`).

```ts
interface PluginManifestV1 {
  $schema?: string;
  manifestVersion: 1;
  id: string;             // ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\.[a-z][a-z0-9-]*){2,}$, ≤128; <org>.<team>.<name>
  version: string;        // strict semver
  displayName: string;    // 1..64
  description?: string;   // ≤500
  publisher: {
    team: string;         // registry rule: must equal id segment 2
    contact: string;      // email
    oncall: string;       // paging alias; plugin health alerts route here
  };
  repository?: string; license?: string;
  engines: {
    pluginApi: SemverRange;   // e.g. "^1.2.0"; restricted syntax: ^ ~ exact >= ">=a <b"; no * or ||
    host?: SemverRange;       // escape hatch for host bugs only
  };
  main: RelativeJsPath;       // server entry; no leading /, no ".."
  browser?: RelativeJsPath;   // required iff a custom visualization exists
  runtime?: {
    kind?: "node";
    isolation?: "process" | "process-per-tenant";   // default "process"
    resources?: {
      memoryMb?: number;             // 64..4096, default 256   (>1024 needs admin approval)
      invocationTimeoutMs?: number;  // 100..600000, default 30000 (>120000 needs approval)
      maxConcurrency?: number;       // 1..256, default 16
      tmpDiskMb?: number;            // 0..2048, default 0 (no scratch disk)
      storageQuotaMb?: number;       // 0..1024, default 10, per tenant
    };
  };
  activation?: {
    onStartup?: boolean;           // default false (lazy). MUST be true if services or scheduledJobs are contributed
    idleTimeoutSeconds?: number;   // 0..86400, default 900; 0 = never idle-unload
  };
  contributes: {                   // at least one key, each array minItems 1
    dataSources?:    (Base & { connectionSchema: ObjSchema; parametersSchema?: ObjSchema;
                       capabilities?: ("filterPushdown"|"projectionPushdown"|"sortPushdown"|
                                       "limitPushdown"|"incremental"|"testConnection")[] })[];
    transforms?:     (Base & { optionsSchema?: ObjSchema; inputs?: { min?: 1..8; max?: 1..8 };
                       deterministic?: boolean /* host may cache */ })[];
    visualizations?: (Base & { mode: "spec"|"custom"; optionsSchema?: ObjSchema;
                       fields: { role: string; displayName?: string; acceptedTypes: DataType[];
                                 required?: boolean; multiple?: boolean }[];   // 1..16
                       maxRows?: number /* ≤200000, default 50000 */ })[];
    exporters?:      (Base & { mimeType: string; fileExtension: string; optionsSchema?: ObjSchema;
                       maxOutputMb?: number /* ≤1024, default 100 */ })[];
    commands?:       (Base & { argsSchema?: ObjSchema; requiredRole: "viewer"|"editor"|"admin";
                       surfaces: ("reportToolbar"|"reportContextMenu"|"adminConsole"|"api")[] })[];
    scheduledJobs?:  (Base & { defaultSchedule: string /* 5-field cron, UTC */;
                       scope: "global"|"tenant"; maxRuntimeSeconds?: number /* ≤3600 */ })[];
    services?:       { id: string /* same pattern as pluginId */; version: Semver; description?: string;
                       methods: Record<string /* camelCase */, { params: ObjSchema; result: Schema;
                                                                 idempotent?: boolean }> }[];
  };
  permissions?: {
    permission: "network.fetch"|"secrets.read"|"data.query"|"events.subscribe"|"storage.kv"|"ui.frontend";
    scope?: string[];   // REQUIRED for the first four, FORBIDDEN for the last two
    reason: string;     // 10..300 chars, shown to the approving admin
  }[];
  dependencies?: Record<PluginId, SemverRange>;   // ≤16
  configuration?: ObjSchema;                       // properties may carry x-scope / x-secret
  state?: { schemaVersion: number };               // version of snapshotState() payload
}

type Base = { id: string /* ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\.[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*$, ≤64 */; displayName: string;
              description?: string; deprecated?: { message: string; replacement?: string } };
type DataType = "string"|"integer"|"float"|"decimal"|"boolean"|"date"|"timestamp"|"duration"|"binary"|"json";

// ObjSchema / Schema: a restricted JSON Schema subset. Allowed keywords only: type, title,
// description, default, enum, minimum, maximum, minLength, maxLength, pattern,
// format(date|date-time|email|uri|hostname|duration), items, minItems, maxItems, properties,
// required, additionalProperties:false. Plus in `configuration`:
//   x-scope: "global"|"tenant"|"report"   – narrowest level the key may be set at
//   x-secret: true                        – stored in vault, read only via ictx.secrets
// No $ref, no remote schemas, no oneOf/anyOf. That keeps the admin UI's form generator simple.
```

**Scope formats:**
- `network.fetch`: `https://[*.]host[:port][/path*]`. HTTPS only; `*` allowed only as the leftmost label.
- `secrets.read`: secret names.
- `data.query`: host dataset IDs.
- `events.subscribe`: event names from the API version's event catalog.

**Checks the registry does that the schema can't:**
1. `publisher.team` matches the ID and is a real team.
2. Contribution IDs are unique within the plugin. The fully qualified ID is `<pluginId>/<contributionId>`.
3. `engines.pluginApi` overlaps a host-supported API range.
4. Event names and dataset IDs exist.
5. `main`/`browser` exist in the package.
6. The package's SHA-256 digest matches its signature.
7. A permission diff against the installed version triggers re-approval (§5.4).
8. Plugins using `process-per-tenant` can't contribute `services`.

**Example:**
```json
