## 1. Component map

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Host                                                             │
│                                                                  │
│  Registry ──── Resolver ──── Activation Scheduler                │
│     │           (DAG,          (lazy, topological)               │
│     │            SemVer)                                         │
│     │                                                            │
│  Extension Point Tables ◄──── Contribution Index (from manifests) │
│     │                                                            │
│  Capability Broker ──── Permission Evaluator ──── Audit Log      │
│     │                                                            │
│  Supervisor ──── Resource Governor ──── Circuit Breaker          │
│     │                                                            │
│  ═══════════════ RPC / Data Plane ═══════════════                │
│     │ control: CBOR envelopes  │ data: Arrow IPC, credit-based   │
└─────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
      │
 ┌────┴────┐  ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐        ┌──────────────────┐
 │ worker  │  │ worker  │  │ process │        │ browser iframe   │
 │ plugin  │  │ plugin  │  │ plugin  │        │ (view half)      │
 └─────────┘  └─────────┘  └─────────┘        └──────────────────┘
```

Note the browser iframe: a reporting tool has custom visualizations, so there are **two** sandboxes. A plugin can have a server half (`main`), a browser half (`browser`), or both. They're separate isolation domains with separate permission sets and they communicate only through the host.

