## 7. What the five teams get

Because the constraint is *five teams shipping next quarter*, these are part of the architecture, not follow-on work:

**`@reporting/plugin-api`** — types + thin client shims. No host internals. This is the only thing plugins depend on.

**`@reporting/plugin-test-kit`** — an in-memory host harness. Run a plugin through discovery → activate → query → deactivate without the real application, assert on emitted batches, inject faults (timeout, abort, credit starvation, revoked capability).

**`@reporting/plugin-conformance`** — a suite every plugin runs in its own CI. This is the mechanism that keeps the contract honest across five independent codebases:
- manifest validates; declared contributions match code registrations
- `activate` completes within budget; no eager network I/O
- abort is honored within 1s at every `AbortSignal` site
- deadline is respected; `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` thrown, not hung
- **no reuse of a transferred batch buffer**
- `deactivate` releases everything; no handles after teardown
- declared pushdown capabilities actually produce pushed-down queries
- errors are `PluginError` with sane `code`/`retryable`
- no undeclared egress attempts (broker in strict mode fails the test)

**`create-reporting-plugin`** — scaffolds a working plugin per extension point with CI, conformance wired in, and a hot-reload dev loop.

**Observability, per-plugin, day one** — `plugin.activate.duration`, `plugin.call.duration{method}`, `plugin.call.errors{code}`, `plugin.batch.rows`, `plugin.batch.bytes`, `plugin.net.bytes`, `plugin.memory.heapUsed`, `plugin.breaker.state`. Traces propagate `traceparent` through the RPC envelope, so a slow report flame-graphs straight into the responsible plugin. Logs are structured-only and attributed; free-text is rate-limited and unindexed.

---

## 8. Recommended build order

| Phase | Deliverable | Unblocks |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Manifest schema, registry + state machine, in-process tier, `plugin-api` v2.0 frozen | Teams write manifests and stub plugins |
| 2 | Worker tier, capability broker, net/secrets/storage capabilities | Teams write real server-side logic |
| 3 | Arrow data plane + credit flow control, `DataSourceProvider` | Connector teams go full speed |
| 4 | Browser sandbox, `VisualizationProvider`, `renderStatic` | Viz teams go full speed |
| 5 | Process tier, resource governor, circuit breaker, quarantine | Production readiness |
| 6 | Conformance kit, test kit, scaffolder, API linter | Quality gate before GA |

Freeze `plugin-api` v2.0 at the end of phase 1 even though the host is incomplete — teams need a stable target more than they need a complete one, and additive MINORs cover the gap.

